    'Founded in 1676, this congregation is the oldest religious organization in Salem County, and the 1772 meetinghouse that stands here is the oldest house of worship in the city. Its exterior has changed almost nothing since construction, and the interior embodies the Quaker principle of expectant silence — many visitors describe the experience of sitting inside as a sudden involuntary stillness, as though the room itself is listening. During the Revolution, British troops encamped here, lending the space a doubled history of both occupation and sanctuary.',
    ARRAY['https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500530855697-b586d89ba3ee?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=80', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500534314209-a25ddb2bd429?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=80']::TEXT[],
