    'Salt Springs State Park preserves a stand of old-growth hemlocks rising over the Silver Creek gorge — one of the largest remaining virgin hemlock groves in Pennsylvania. Visitors describe the grove as cathedral-like, with light filtering through the old canopy in a way that several compare to entering a dim church nave. The hemlock-shaded gorge has an unusual coolness and quiet that many describe as deeply settling, while the ancient scale of the trees prompts what some call an awareness of deep time.',
