    'verified',
    'Pithole City rose from empty farmland to a metropolis of 15,000 people in a matter of months in 1865, then collapsed just as fast, its entire existence lasting barely 500 days. Today, visitors walk mowed paths through what was once Pennsylvania''s third-busiest post office — and find nothing. The absence is itself the thing: no foundations, no ruins, only the grass and the silence of a place where an entire city used to be. Many visitors report a strong sense of presence or unease that they attribute to the scale of what is missing.',
    ARRAY['https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1496307042754-b4aa456c4a2d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=80', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500530855697-b586d89ba3ee?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=80']::TEXT[],
