    'The Drake Well site along Oil Creek marks where the modern petroleum industry began in 1859 — a moment that reshaped the world. The park and museum grounds have an unusually reflective quality: the reconstructed derrick beside the creek, the wide-open oil country landscape, and the weight of historical significance create an atmosphere that many visitors describe as profoundly still. Several note that standing at the spot of the original Drake Well produces a feeling that is less celebratory than solemn.',
