    'Hexenkopf — German for ''witch''s head'' — is a glacial boulder formation in Northampton County long associated with unusual phenomena. The site was used in Native American rituals, later became part of Pennsylvania Dutch witch lore, and today generates accounts from visitors of strange glowing effects, disorientation, and an uncanny pressure in the surrounding area. The rock features a mineral coating that can appear to glow under certain light.',
